<title>FRANCE: Cerus shares suspended again.</title>
<headline>Cerus shares suspended again.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in holding company Cerus were suspended limit-up for a second time on Monday morning, the French stockmarkets association SBF said.</p>
<p>An SBF spokeswoman said trading in the stock would resume at 0840 GMT with a new ceiling of 143.90 francs.</p>
<p>The newspaper Les Echos reported on Monday that CGIP was discussing a buyout of Cerus from Italian industrialist Carlo De Benedetti. Cerus, which owns 28 percent of car parts manufacturer Valeo, and CGIP declined comment.</p>
</text>
